\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces The full ensemble of measured weak-lensing suppression curves $S_i(\ell ,z_{\rm  s})=C_\ell ^{\kappa \kappa }(\theta _{\rm  astro}^i)/C_\ell ^{\kappa \kappa ,{\rm  DMO}}$ for 99 SB35 Sobol realizations at five source planes (labeled $z_{\rm  s}$ in each panel), computed against a single fixed, paired DMO skeleton and colored by each run's group gas fraction $f_{\rm  gas}$; the near-black solid/dashed lines mark the ensemble median and 95\% envelope. The ensemble brackets both suppression and enhancement relative to the paired DMO trace, and the spread narrows toward higher $z_{\rm  s}$ as the low-redshift baryonic signal is diluted by feedback-free structure along the line of sight. The $x$-axis is capped at $\ell _{\rm  max,trust}=1.5\times 10^4$, above which CIC aliasing dominates the run-to-run scatter. The $z_{\rm  s}=0.5$ panel's $y$-axis is fixed at $[0.78,1.18]$ for readability across all five panels, which visibly clips the highest-enhancement curves and the top of the 95\% envelope near $\ell \sim 10^4$; the $\approx 0.80$--$1.24$ range quoted in the text is the full unclipped envelope measured from the underlying array, not what is directly visible within this panel's plotted range.}}{6}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:transfer_ensemble}{{1}{6}{The full ensemble of measured weak-lensing suppression curves $S_i(\ell ,\zs )=C_\ell ^{\kappa \kappa }(\theta _{\rm astro}^i)/C_\ell ^{\kappa \kappa ,{\rm DMO}}$ for 99 SB35 Sobol realizations at five source planes (labeled $\zs $ in each panel), computed against a single fixed, paired DMO skeleton and colored by each run's group gas fraction $\fgas $; the near-black solid/dashed lines mark the ensemble median and 95\% envelope. The ensemble brackets both suppression and enhancement relative to the paired DMO trace, and the spread narrows toward higher $\zs $ as the low-redshift baryonic signal is diluted by feedback-free structure along the line of sight. The $x$-axis is capped at $\ell _{\rm max,trust}=1.5\times 10^4$, above which CIC aliasing dominates the run-to-run scatter. The $\zs =0.5$ panel's $y$-axis is fixed at $[0.78,1.18]$ for readability across all five panels, which visibly clips the highest-enhancement curves and the top of the 95\% envelope near $\ell \sim 10^4$; the $\approx 0.80$--$1.24$ range quoted in the text is the full unclipped envelope measured from the underlying array, not what is directly visible within this panel's plotted range}{figure.1}{}}
