\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces The N-template ladder (headline result). Left: residual $|\Delta S_8|/\sigma _{S_8}$ (LSST-Y10) after marginalizing $N$ baryon templates, median and 95th-percentile across 216 runs, at three $\ell _{\rm  max}$ cuts (log-$y$ axis; the vertical red line marks $N=2$). The residual collapses by roughly two orders of magnitude between $N=0$ and $N=2$ and then flattens. Right: the corresponding $\sigma _{S_8}$ inflation relative to the no-baryon floor, which grows monotonically and near-linearly with $N$ well past the point where the bias is already removed.}}{9}{figure.4}\protected@file@percent }
